Version 2.4.2 is a very small update to the previous version, fixing a bug
causing some voices to crash upon startup, which in practice only
manifested itself when the plugin was build as a VST3 and no preset
was loaded before playing the first note.

Fixes:
- An uninitialized value for the expoential portamento caused arbitrary
  voices to crash, emitting a large DC value, in certain cases.
  - More specifically, when a VST3 plugin was played without loading
    a preset first. (Although there is actually no connection between the
    bug and loading a preset, so this is just an observation, which seems to 
    be consistent between Reaper and Cubase though).
  - There have been no reports of this problem for LV2, but that would
    seem to be more by chance than anything else, as the DSP code
    is identical for all versions of the plugin.

Other Changes:
- Removed the knob drop shadow in the UI as it didn't really have the intended
  visual impact and rather cluttered up the surrounding value arc.

As usual, a companion version 2.4.2z has been tagged on the Zynthian branch,
which supports the graphic envelope and filter display features in the Zynthian
UI.
